From: Floe contributors <recipe@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] windows: limit legacy secure CRT macros to old MSVC

MinGW does not define _MSC_VER, so the preprocessor treats it as zero in
the version comparison. This incorrectly enables the legacy wcscpy_s and
wcscat_s macros, even though MinGW provides these functions. When windows.h
is included afterwards, the statement macro breaks the wcscpy_s expression
in stralign.h's ua_wcscpy_s inline function.

Only provide the compatibility macros for the old MSVC versions that need
them. Leave MinGW's secure CRT functions and the MSVC paths unchanged.

---
 libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h b/libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h
--- a/libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h
+++ b/libvpl/src/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 #define MAX_PLUGIN_PATH 4096
 #define MAX_PLUGIN_NAME 4096
 
-#if _MSC_VER < 1400
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) && _MSC_VER < 1400
     #define wcscpy_s(to, to_size, from) \
         (void)(to_size);                \
         wcscpy(to, from)
